---
name: fight-ai-auth
description: Why fight-ai auth is Google OIDC inside FastAPI with a cookie (2026-09-29) — rejected alternatives and user's product choices.
metadata:
  type: project
---

On 2026-09-29 the user chose Google sign-in built into FastAPI (Authlib, Starlette signed session cookie, `users` table) over Clerk/Auth0, Tailscale Serve, Cloudflare Access and oauth2-proxy.

User's product choices: three roles viewer < labeller < admin; **any Google account auto-joins as viewer** (so the OAuth consent screen must be "In production", not Testing); admins manage users on an in-app `/users` page; disable, never delete.

**Why:** `<video src>` and EventSource can't send an Authorization header, so hosted-provider bearer tokens break video and SSE; Cloudflare's free 100 MB body cap breaks 53–474 MB uploads; Tailscale needs every viewer on the tailnet. MVP budget is $0.
**How to apply:** don't re-propose token-based auth or a cross-origin frontend. See [[fight-ai-hosting-constraints]] for where the app can be hosted.
